1.1
-feature: External secret providers - resolve credential secrets from HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, Azure Key Vault, Google Cloud Secret Manager and CyberArk Conjur
-feature: Pluggable CredentialProvider driver interface and registry so additional secret stores can be added without changing the storage or UI layer
-feature: New 'credential_providers' table storing provider instances; per-connection secrets (tokens, keys, client secrets) encrypted with the Cacti core secret functions
-feature: New 'Secret Providers' management page (list/add/edit/enable/disable/delete) with a per-provider 'Test Connection' self-check
-feature: Per-credential 'Secret Provider' selector; a provider-backed secret field stores a non-sensitive reference the provider resolves at poll time instead of the secret itself
-feature: Support more than one provider instance of the same or different types side by side, mixing local and external storage per credential
-feature: Reference syntax with an optional '#key' selector to pull a single field from a JSON secret, and dotted paths into nested JSON
-feature: Per-request resolution cache so a poll does not repeatedly round-trip to a store; failures fail closed and are logged without leaking secrets
-feature: Add a 'provider_id' column to the 'credentials' table and an idempotent upgrade path for existing installations
-feature: Add a 'Secret Providers' menu pick and breadcrumb navigation, gated on the core Users/Groups permission

1.0
-feature: Initial release of the Credentials plugin
-feature: Tier 1 credential types - SNMP v1/v2c Community, SNMP v3 (USM), Username/Password, SSH
-feature: Tier 2 credential types - Bearer/API Token, API Key, GitHub PAT, OAuth 2.0 Client Credentials, HTTP Basic Auth
-feature: Tier 3 credential types - WMI, IPMI/Redfish, Database, VMware/vCenter, TLS Client Certificate
-feature: Store credentials in the 'credentials' table with name, description, user_id, enabled, create_date, last_updated and JSON properties columns
-feature: Render each type's required and optional fields with tooltips using the Cacti Form API
-feature: Encrypt all sensitive fields with the Cacti core secret functions and never render stored secrets in clear text
-feature: Place the 'Credentials' menu pick below 'User Domains' (1.2.x) or 'Login Providers' (develop/1.3+)
-feature: Gate credentials.php access on the core Users/Groups permission
-feature: Warn with a jQueryUI dialog about losing stored data before switching the Credential Type of an existing credential
